Entries for the Louisiana QSO Party used by in-state (Louisiana) stations
The 64 Louisiana parishes (each its own multiplier), the US states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC countries other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier, not entries here.
The parish file comes FIRST, so a parish code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before s50.dom: the rules count States, and NY4I's default on issue 122 counts DC as Maryland.
Louisiana itself is not a multiplier for an in-state entrant ("States (other than Louisiana)"): the class refuses it.
s50.dom is included BEFORE p13.dom: p13 also spells Newfoundland LA, and the first alias added wins, so LA stays Louisiana.
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line): rule 8.2.3 counts the 13 provinces, Maritime regions not separately.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE louisiana_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
INCLUDE FILE p13.dom
Nl = NF,LB
